{% block content %}
  <main>
    <h1 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">A quick, plain-language rundown: what data I keep, why, and how you can see or delete it.</p>

    <div class="policy">
      <p class="updated">Last updated: October 27, 2026</p>

      <h3>Data controller</h3>
      <p>The data controller is the creator of Δέσε Κορδόνια.</p>

      <h3>What data I collect</h3>
      <p>
        If you're just browsing the site, I don't ask you for any personal data. The infrastructure
        providers I use (Cloudflare, Render, Supabase) may log technical details such as your IP
        address, as part of the normal operation/security of their servers. I don't have access to
        those logs and don't use them to identify you. Whatever the site remembers about you without
        an account (likes, saved articles, pace, city) stays <strong>locally in your browser</strong>;
        see "What is stored in your browser" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you create an account (the first sign-in is always with an email "magic link"), I keep: your
        <strong>email</strong>, optionally your <strong>name</strong> and a short <strong>bio</strong> if you
        fill them in, and whether you want to receive the <strong>newsletter</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Sign-in with Face ID / Touch ID / fingerprint (passkey), optional.</strong>
        Your face or fingerprint <strong>never leaves your device</strong>: the device itself does the
        check, and all that reaches me is a public key, which reveals nothing about you. For each
        passkey I keep: its ID and public key, a usage counter (to detect a copied key), how the
        device connects (e.g. USB, Bluetooth), the kind of device (e.g. "iPhone", from your browser),
        when you added it and when you last used it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Password, optional.</strong> If you set a password, I don't store the password itself,
        only a cryptographic fingerprint of it (a scrypt hash with a random salt), from which the
        password cannot be recovered, and the date you last set or changed it.
      </p>
      <p>
        For security, when you take actions on your account (sign in, sign out, change your profile,
        or delete it), I keep a short <strong>security log</strong> with your <strong>IP address</strong>,
        browser (user-agent), and the type of action, to protect the site from abuse (legitimate
        interest). This log is kept for up to <strong>6 months</strong> and then deleted automatically;
        if you delete your account, your email is removed from it immediately.
      </p>

      <h3>How I use it &amp; legal basis</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>To sign you in (with an email magic link, a passkey or a password, whichever you chose) and to remember your profile details, necessary to provide the account you asked for.</li>
        <li>To send you the newsletter, only with your consent, when you opt in.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I don't sell, share, or use your data for advertising.</p>

      <h3>How long I keep it</h3>
      <p>
        Your account details stay stored for as long as your account is active. If you delete your
        account, your email, name, bio, newsletter preference, passkeys and password hash are removed
        from the database immediately. You can also remove a passkey or your password on its own,
        without deleting your account. A minimal entry <strong>without your email</strong> (e.g. IP address and action
        type) may remain in the security log for up to 6 months, then it's deleted automatically.
      </p>

      <h3>Where it's stored</h3>
      <p>Your account data and emails stay within the European Union:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your account (email, name, bio, newsletter preference, passkeys, password hash): database on <a href="https://supabase.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">Supabase</a> (Frankfurt, Germany).</li>
        <li>The server (API) that manages it: <a href="https://render.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">Render</a> (Frankfurt, Germany).</li>
        <li>The security log (IP address, user-agent, action type): in the same Supabase project, auto-deleted after up to 6 months.</li>
        <li>Sign-in &amp; newsletter emails are sent via <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">Resend</a> (Ireland).</li>
        <li>The anonymous like counter, in a separate Supabase project, no personal data.</li>
        <li>Traffic is measured anonymously via <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">GoatCounter</a>, with no cookies and no personal data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Website hosting, weather and map</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The website is served through <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">Cloudflare</a> (Cloudflare, Inc., USA). Like any server, Cloudflare sees your IP address and technical details of the request (for example which page was requested and your browser), in order to deliver the page and protect the website from attacks. I do not use these details to identify you.</li>
        <li>The weather forecast comes from <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">Open-Meteo</a> (OpenMeteo GmbH, Switzerland), directly from your browser, in three places: the "Running weather today" card on the home page, every time you open it; the <a href="kairos-rythmos-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Weather-Adjusted Pace</a> tool, when you use it; and each race's page, when the race is at most 15 days away. The service receives your IP address and the coordinates of a point: on the home page, the city you chose in the tool or, if you haven't chosen one, Athens; in the tool, the city you search for or, if you press "Use my location", your location rounded to about 1 km; on a race page, the race venue. The home page and the race pages never ask for your location. According to its terms, it keeps these logs for up to 90 days. Your location never reaches me; your city and pace are stored only locally in your browser.</li>
        <li>The map on the "<a href="agones-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Races</a>" page loads its map tiles (the images) from the <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--accent);">OpenStreetMap</a> servers (OpenStreetMap Foundation, United Kingdom), directly from your browser, when you open the page. The service receives your IP address, your browser and which part of the map you're viewing, as described in its privacy policy. It doesn't ask for your location and sets no cookies. The map software (Leaflet) is served by this website itself.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What is stored in your browser</h3>
      <p>
        Some features remember your choices in the browser itself (localStorage), not in cookies and
        not on any server. They are stored only when you use the matching feature, never reach me and
        are not shared with anyone:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>dk_liked</code>, <code>dk_likes_local</code>: which articles you liked, so a like isn't counted twice. The shared counter only receives an anonymous +1 or −1, with nothing about you.</li>
        <li><code>dk_saved</code>, <code>dk_saved_sort</code>: the articles you saved and the order you want to see them in.</li>
        <li><code>weatherPace</code>: the pace and city (with its coordinates) you entered in Weather-Adjusted Pace. The "Clear" button in the tool deletes them.</li>
        <li><code>racePace</code>: your goal (pace, or time and distance) for each race, on the race pages.</li>
        <li><code>theme</code>: whether you prefer the light or dark theme.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can delete all of them at any time from your browser settings (clear site data for
        desekordonia.com). In private browsing they are deleted on their own when you close the window.
      </p>

      <h3>Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        I only use one strictly necessary session cookie while you're signed in, so I can recognize you.
        It expires after 7 days or when you sign out. No advertising, profiling, or third-party
        tracking cookies.
      </p>

      <h3>Your rights</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>View and edit your details anytime on the "<a href="account-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">My account</a>" page.</li>
        <li>Delete your account anytime from the same page. This immediately removes your email, name, bio, and newsletter preference from the database; only a temporary entry without your email stays in the security log.</li>
        <li>Unsubscribe from the newsletter via the link in every email.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        For any question about your personal data or this Privacy Policy, you can reach out at
        <a href="mailto:hello@desekordonia.com" style="color:var(--accent);">hello@desekordonia.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
